Substitute back into the Law of Cosines:
\[ c^2 = 349,422.7769 + 321,277.7761 - 109,276.744 \]
\[ c^2 = 561,423.809 \]

Finally, take the square root to find \( c \):
\[ c = \sqrt{561,423.809} \approx 749.28' \]

The closest option to this calculated value is:
\[ \text{Distance } CB = 748.70' \]

